<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!-- Checks the minimap's and the GPS's game-free parts outside the game: the search done whole and in slices, routes
       on a made-up grid of streets, turns, leaving the route and arriving, the view's arithmetic and the map picture.
       Compiles the mod's own files, so it checks exactly what ships. It also checks the bus bays (BayCheck.cs with
       Transport\BusBay.cs): where a bus stands, the curves in and out, and a model bus driven along them. And the taxi called from the
       phone (TaxiCheck.cs with Transport\Taxi\TaxiRules.cs): its charges, its bands, its refusals, and its search. And the rules of the live street
       (StreetCheck.cs with Traffic\Reckless\StreetRules.cs): the horn, the reckless drivers, how often, and what comes of it. And the minimap's
       buildings and water (BaseCheck.cs with Navigation\NavBaseRules.cs): a place on the picture and back, the window at the city's edges,
       outlines, the water grid, the drawing and the kept file. And three small rules
       of the interface and the camera (PolishCheck.cs with Core\GameUi\PanelPlacement.cs, Core\GameUi\BarRule.cs, Camera\CameraWatch.cs and
       Core\OtherModName.cs): where a panel stands beside the game's building box, when a bar is written again, and when the camera
       stands down for another mod's. And the ambulance crew's way as geometry (CrewCheck.cs with People\CrewPath.cs): how near the
       crew comes to a point and to a length of tape, and what a planning's worth of ways costs. And the game-free parts of the work against long frames (HitchCheck.cs and HotSpotCheck.cs with Core\EventHold.cs, Core\WorkRings.cs, Core\HotSpots.cs and Core\SearchPace.cs): handlers kept on the game's events, the session record's rings, the timing of the mod's own scripts by feature and method, when the whole scene may be searched, and (PrewarmCheck.cs, over the sources) that the one-off work of the first seconds after a load is handed to the loading screen or read from the game's own lists. And getting out of the driving school's car (CarExitCheck.cs with Licences\Driving\CarExitRules.cs): the places tried around the car, when a player is stuck half out of it, and when the car may go. And the furnished police station (StationCheck.cs with Law\StationPlan.cs): the walkway check that keeps the counter, the cell and every seat reachable from the door, and how many people the station has. And the tow truck (TowCheck.cs with Traffic\Tow\TowRules.cs): its bed's motion, a wreck drawn along the road and up the bed without a jump, where it stands ahead of a wreck, how long it is said to take, and when it may come and go. And the tech sector's buildings (TechSiteCheck.cs with Tech\Sites\SitePlan.cs and RoomPlans.cs): a data centre's server room by tier and racks, its aisles and walkways, a headquarters' lobby, a tech office's fittings, and which office building is which company's headquarters. And the fit-out of the mod's buildings (FitCheck.cs with FitOut\FitRules.cs, FitPlanner.cs and FitPlanner.Zones.cs): the game's design for a unit round what a building already has, the bare floor given rooms of the building's kind, and the walkway check that keeps every seat, every way out and every part of the floor reached from the door. And whose a car is in a Going Public session (CarCheck.cs with Core\WhoseCar.cs): another player's car is never the player's to tow, impound or bill for, and a car of the traffic pool is asked for only when the game would take an idle one of that very prefab, never one in use by its model. And the build check and the guard against an older game (BuildCheck.cs with Core\GameBuild.cs): which build is older or newer, the member named in a missing member's message, the installed game's build against GameBuild.MadeFor, every member the mod reads in a method of its own found in the installed game's assemblies, those an older game lacked named only in the guard's files, and every guarded entry point still guarded. Run: dotnet run -c Release (from this folder).
       Exit code 0 = all checks passed. With the path of a file of lane points as its argument it also times the search
       and the picture on that city (see the README, "Minimap and GPS"). -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <Nullable>disable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>disable</ImplicitUsings>
    <RootNamespace>RealLifeOverhaul</RootNamespace>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
